# M-D3: keep Docker build context (Fly API + worker + web/admin) tight — avoid
# uploading the whole monorepo, secrets, and app bundles unrelated to the API
# image. Each Dockerfile still COPYs only what it needs; this just shrinks the
# tarball sent to the builder and keeps sensitive files out of the layer cache.

# ---- VCS / IDE / OS noise -------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.vscode
.idea
.cursor
.claude
.agents
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---- Dependency / build output (each stage restores what it needs) --------
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/dist
**/build
**/out
**/coverage
**/.nyc_output
**/.parcel-cache

# ---- Test / lint / TypeScript intermediates -------------------------------
**/*.log
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.map
**/npm-debug.log*
**/yarn-debug.log*
**/yarn-error.log*
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/*.spec.ts.snap

# ---- Env / secrets (must never leak into an image) ------------------------
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.*.example
secrets/
firebase/
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
credentials.json
service-account*.json

# ---- Apps + assets not needed inside API/worker images --------------------
apps/mobile
apps/web/public/uploads
apps/admin/public/uploads

# ---- Docs / markdown / audits / prompts (not needed at runtime) -----------
docs
**/README.md
**/CHANGELOG.md
**/CONTRIBUTING.md
*.md
MASTERPROJECTAUDITPROMPT.md
newPrompt.md
new_dataprompt.md
prompt.md

# ---- Local infra + editor artefacts ---------------------------------------
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.prod.reference.yml
compose.prod.env.example
infra/nginx/ssl

# ---- Terraform / infra state ----------------------------------------------
**/.terraform
**/terraform.tfstate
**/terraform.tfstate.backup
**/*.tfvars

# ---- Misc -----------------------------------------------------------------
tmp
.tmp
.cache
